//! Minimal safe RAII wrapper around the [DiligentEngine](https://github.com/DiligentGraphics/DiligentEngine)
//! (DiligentCore) C API generated by `diligent-sys`.
//!
//! # Scope
//!
//! The wrapper covers the resource surface a wgpu backend replacement needs
//! (M1 milestone of the "wgpu -> Diligent" migration):
//!
//! * [`EngineFactoryD3D12`] - factory entry point (`Diligent_GetEngineFactoryD3D12`).
//! * [`RenderDevice`] - device object creation (`IRenderDevice`): buffers,
//!   textures (`create_texture`), texture views (`create_texture_view`),
//!   samplers (`create_sampler`), shaders from HLSL (`create_shader`) or
//!   bytecode/SPIR-V (`create_shader_spirv`), PRS, PSO, fence.
//! * [`DeviceContext`] - immediate context state + draw commands (`IDeviceContext`).
//! * [`SwapChain`] - presentation (`ISwapChain`).
//! * [`Buffer`], [`Texture`], [`TextureView`], [`Sampler`], [`Shader`],
//!   [`PipelineResourceSignature`], [`PipelineState`],
//!   [`ShaderResourceBinding`], [`Fence`] - the resource objects.
//! * [`format`] - the bidirectional wgpu <-> Diligent texture format mapping
//!   table, including the documented Depth24Plus landing and the sRGB
//!   dual-view helper.
//!
//! Everything else in `diligent-sys` remains reachable through
//! [`diligent_sys::bindings`](diligent_sys::bindings) for escape hatches.
//!
//! # Memory model
//!
//! Every wrapped Diligent interface is reference counted (see
//! `IObject::AddRef/Release` in the engine). All owning wrappers
//! ([`Buffer`], [`Shader`], [`Texture`], [`Sampler`], [`PipelineState`], ...)
//! call `Release` on `Drop`, so leaking raw engine objects is not possible
//! through this API. Ownership can be shared explicitly with
//! [`Handle::add_ref`] (COM `AddRef`, the primitive for the
//! `WgpuWrapper`/Arc cloning semantics of M1b). Handles returned
//! **without** a reference count increment are wrapped as [`NonOwning`]
//! (e.g. `SwapChain::current_back_buffer_rtv`,
//! `Texture::get_default_view`) and never released.
//!
//! # Threading
//!
//! No wrapper implements `Send`/`Sync`. In particular, a [`DeviceContext`]
//! must only ever be used from the thread it was created on - Diligent
//! command recording is not thread safe. The device and resource objects
//! (`IRenderDevice`, `IBuffer`, `ITexture`, `ISampler`, `IPipelineState`, ...)
//! are thread safe in Diligent, but this crate keeps them pinned to their
//! creating thread until a deliberate opt-in; cross-thread usage requires
//! `unsafe` access through `as_raw()` and is the caller's responsibility.
//!
//! # Examples
//!
//! See `examples/triangle.rs` (winit 0.30 + D3D12) for the full
//! PRS -> PSO -> SRB -> draw -> present round trip.

